      "id": "sol.ahsme-1952-p26.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let \\(u=r+\\frac{1}{r}.\\) Expanding \\(u^3\\) gives \\[ r^3+\\frac1{r^3}=u^3-3u. \\] Since \\(u^2=3,\\) this becomes \\(u(u^2-3)=0.\\)\n\nThus the value is \\(0,\\) so the correct answer is C.",
